# Network boot: where a network-booted machine loads its root from (build.sh
# signs it into the UKI). Copy to netboot.conf (not tracked by git). Sourced
# as bash.
#
# NETROOT_URL: the share of the distribution servers, <SERVER_URL>/ of their
# server.conf (server/server.conf.example). The initrd fetches roothash,
# root.verity and root.img from there:
#   NETROOT_URL=http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/
#   -> safespace.netroot=http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/
#      and the initrd fetches .../root.img and .../root.verity
#
# An IP address needs no DNS at all. A host name works too: the initrd resolves
# it with the DNS servers from its DHCP lease (see NETBOOT.md, "A host name
# instead of an IP address").
# Several URLs (space separated) are tried in order: a name with an address as
# fallback, or several distribution servers:
#   NETROOT_URL="http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/ http://10.0.0.2/safespace/"
# The URLs are part of the signed kernel command line; changing them means
# rebuilding the image. Without NETROOT_URL a build boots from sticks only.
NETROOT_URL=http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/
